my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
line one
line two
line three
line four
line five
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{`a jumps to the exact mark position (line and column)},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/mark_jump_backtick`

**ma** sets mark 'a' at the current position. **\`a** jumps back to the exact line and column where the mark was set.

**Keys:** `4l` then `ma` then `jjj` then `` `a ``

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0

**after_move_right.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 4 (on ' ' space in "line one")

**after_set_mark.png**
- Mark 'a' set at line 1, col 4
- Cursor still at line 1, col 4

**after_move_down.png**
- Cursor at line 4, col 4 (moved down 3 lines with `jjj`)

**after_backtick_a.png**
- Cursor back at line 1, col 4 (exact mark position)
- `` `a `` restores both line and column
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('4l');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_right');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ma');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_set_mark');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('jjj');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_down');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('`a');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_backtick_a');
    },
}
